facts:
A fair coin has equally likely heads and tails. A fair die has equally likely numbers. On a fairly spun spinner, each distinct label on one equal sector has the same chance.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.3);
\foreach \a in {0,90,180,270} {\draw (0,0) -- (\a:1.3);}
\node at (45:0.75) {$A$};
\node at (135:0.75) {$B$};
\node at (225:0.75) {$C$};
\node at (315:0.75) {$D$};
\node[font=\small] at (0,-1.85) {equal sectors};
\node[font=\small] at (0,-2.35) {equally likely};
\begin{scope}[shift={(5,0)}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.3);
\foreach \a in {90,180,270} {\draw (0,0) -- (\a:1.3);}
\node at (0:0.8) {$A$};
\node at (135:0.75) {$B$};
\node at (225:0.75) {$C$};
\node[font=\small] at (0,-1.85) {sectors not equal};
\node[font=\small] at (0,-2.35) {not equally likely};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Each spinner is spun fairly and its label is recorded.
(a) Seven equal sectors are labelled green, green, green, blue, blue, red and yellow.
(b) Six equal sectors are labelled sun, sun, moon, moon, star and star.
List the possible recorded results and decide whether they are equally likely.

(a) G = green, B = blue, R = red, Y = yellow.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.7);
\foreach \i in {0,...,6} {\draw (0,0)--({90-\i*360/7}:1.7);}
\foreach \i/\lab in {0/G,1/G,2/G,3/B,4/B,5/R,6/Y} {\node at ({90-(\i+0.5)*360/7}:1.12) {\lab};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(b)
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\foreach \a in {30,90,150,210,270,330} {\draw (0,0)--(\a:2);}
\foreach \a/\lab in {60/sun,0/sun,300/moon,240/moon,180/star,120/star} {\node at (\a:1.25) {\lab};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A spinner is spun fairly. Leaf covers half the wheel; acorn and flower each cover one quarter.
List the possible results. Are all three equally likely? Which two have the same chance?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\draw (0,-2)--(0,2);
\draw (0,0)--(2,0);
\node at (-1,0) {leaf};
\node at (0.85,0.85) {acorn};
\node at (0.85,-0.85) {flower};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A spinner has four equal sectors labelled $3$, $6$, $9$ and $12$. It is spun fairly and its number is recorded.
(a) List all the outcomes and say whether they are equally likely.
(b) Mia lists the sample space as $\{3,6,9,12\}$. Noah lists it as $\{12,9,6,3\}$. Who is correct?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.5);
\draw (-1.5,0)--(1.5,0);
\draw (0,-1.5)--(0,1.5);
\node at (45:0.9) {$3$};
\node at (135:0.9) {$6$};
\node at (225:0.9) {$9$};
\node at (315:0.9) {$12$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A fair spinner has six equal sectors labelled $A,A,A,B,B,C$.
(a) List all the sector outcomes and the sample space.
(b) Sam says the sample space must include $A$ three times. Is Sam correct?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.6);
\foreach \a in {30,90,150,210,270,330} {\draw (0,0)--(\a:1.6);}
\foreach \a/\lab in {60/A,0/A,300/A,240/B,180/B,120/C} {\node at (\a:1) {$\lab$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
